<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Niger Delta</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niger-river">Niger</a> Delta is the wide coastal delta of the Niger River in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a>, a region of creeks, mangroves and fertile soils. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benin-empire">Benin Empire</a>'s agricultural base in the delta region and surrounding forest produced yams, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palm-oil">palm oil</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kola-nut">kola nuts</a>. These products supported both local consumption and long-distance trade.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/niger-delta.jpg" alt="Niger Delta" width="320" height="328" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: NASA · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nigerdelta_NASA.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
